0..69 Comment "// Function extensionality from univalence, Voevodsky\'s argument: the"
70..144 Comment "// diagonal of the path space of `b` is an equivalence, so `ua` makes it a"
145..218 Comment "// path between types, and carrying a function out of the path space back"
219..292 Comment "// along that path is injective. The two ends of the path space read back"
293..368 Comment "// alike along it, both the identity, so they are one function, and any map"
369..445 Comment "// into the path space gives a path between its two ends. A homotopy is such"
446..523 Comment "// a map, and its ends read back as the two functions. The HoTT book\'s § 4.9"
524..597 Comment "// credits the argument to Voevodsky and reworks it through weak function"
598..616 Comment "// extensionality."
618..692 Comment "/// The diagonal of the path space: a point, to itself, along reflexivity."
